<figure id="S5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9. </span>
Overview of model performance using the <span id="S5.T9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Query-to-Doc CoT</span> query rewriting approach on the chunked-document version of CRUMB. The <span id="S5.T9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Query-to-Doc CoT</span> approach uses a generated relevant document created based on the original query as the rewritten query. We use three metrics: normalized discounted cumulative gain at 10 (nDCG@10), recall at 100 (R@100), and recall at 1000 (R@1000). The last row shows the average (mean) value of each metric across all the tasks.
</figcaption>
